  "bodyText": "Worship\n\n“Sing to the Lord a new song; sing to the Lord, all the earth.\n\nSing to the Lord, praise his name; proclaim his salvation day after day.\n\nDeclare his glory among the nations,his marvelous deeds among all peoples.”\n\nPsalm 96:1-3\n\nJoin us at 10:45 AM every Sunday to worship with us or view our live stream below!\n\nWhat to expect on Sunday\n\nIf you would like to have an overview of our Sunday service, click the button below!\n\nWorship Leaders\n\nThe Worship Ministry at FBCM understands that Christian worship is a lifestyle centered around responding to the revealed God of the Bible. Worship is also a series of interconnected actions like prayer, fellowship, giving full attention to the Bible, singing, and observing communion.\n\nWhen we gather, worship leaders help us by:\n\nGreeting people as they enter\n\nSinging and playing a variety of instruments\n\nSupporting through technical arts (sound, slides, livestream, etc.)\n\nLeading in prayer & scripture reading\n\nServing communion\n\nPraise Team & Instrumentalists\n\nOur Praise Team consists of longtime church members, college interns, and newer friends who sing, and play a variety of instruments. Instruments played in worship range from the ukulele to the organ!\n\nHandbell Choir\n\nA unique aspect of our church is our hand bell choir, always looking for new members. We believe that music is an important part of our spiritual life and look forward to making beautiful music with you.\n\nGet Involved\n\nIf you wish to be a part of our ministry on Sunday mornings, contact us!\n\nCynthia Smith\n\nWorship Arts Director\n\ncynthia[at]fbcmuncie.org\n\nMolly Flodder\n\nCCT Worship Coordinator\n\nworship[at]fbcmuncie.org\n\n[Button] View Sunday Livestream -> https://www.youtube.com/@FbcmuncieOrg/streams\n\n[Button] What to expect -> https://www.fbcmuncie.org/what-to-expect",
